# 1.7.0
- Removed: the older jQuery copies nothing loaded: jquery-3.7.1.js, jquery-3.7.1.min.js,
  jquery-migrate-3.4.1.min.js and jquery-ui-1.10.3.custom.min.js (jQuery UI 1.10.3 has known
  vulnerabilities). design/standard/javascript/ holds one release of each library: jQuery 4.0.0,
  jQuery Migrate 4.0.2 and jQuery UI 1.14.2. A template or an ezjscore.ini of a site that names one
  of the removed files loads nothing for it: name ezjsc::jquery / ezjsc::jqueryUI or the shipped file.
- Updated: on a siteaccess that requires a sign-in (RequireUserLogin=true, normally the admin),
  ezjscore/call needs a signed-in user: site.ini.append.php no longer lists it in
  [SiteAccessSettings] AnonymousAccessList. Front ends are not affected.
- Updated: the ajax uploader keeps the stored file on the server between its steps. The location
  form carries a one-time token, bound to the user and the upload target and valid for an hour,
  instead of a path; the file is taken only from the storage directory; every step checks the
  handler's canUpload(). A location form override replaces the UploadFile field with UploadToken;
  the admin designs of Exponential 6.0.15 carry the new form, so on an older kernel override
  ajaxuploader/location.tpl the same way.
  [ezjscServer_ezajaxuploader] RequirePolicy (disabled) can also ask for ezjscore/call with the
  function list ezajaxuploader.
- Updated: ezjsc::search passes only positive integer ids to the search engine (subtrees, sections,
  class attributes, the time limit) and looks up a class named by its identifier to its id; the
  offset and the limit are at least 0 and 1.
- Updated: German translation of the uploader's new message.
- Updated: Version 1.7.0 in ezinfo.php and extension.xml.


# 1.6.0
- Added: [ezjscServer_<group>] RequirePolicy (ezjscore.ini). Not set: Functions[] is checked as
  before. disabled: not checked. enabled: checked, and a request whose calls are all refused is
  answered with 403 Forbidden. ezjscnode ships RequirePolicy=disabled, so nothing changes until a
  site switches it on (FunctionList[]=ezjscnode for the policy limitation).
  ezjscServerRouter::getInstance() takes an optional fourth argument that is set to why a call was
  refused, and ezjscServerRouter::refusedStatus() gives the HTTP status for those refusals.
  Derived from LoveStack (mugoweb/ezpublish-legacy, commit aa307a7ff3), with thanks to Mugo Web.
- Added: the ezjsc::search server function sorts eZ Find results by ezfind.ini
  [SearchSettings] SortBy[] (field => asc|desc). settings/ezfind.ini.append.php ships
  SortBy[published]=desc, the order search always used. Derived from LoveStack (commits
  3d2d337b0d and 3af1ec3aee), with thanks to Mugo Web.
- Updated: the ajax uploader checks an uploaded image by its content against the image types
  the installation allows before the file is stored (derived from LoveStack commit c8e45fced7),
  and its location form asks for an alternative text when the image's class requires one
  (derived from LoveStack commit a28863d9c0). Both use the image checks of the Exponential 6.0.15
  kernel (eZContentUpload::imageUploadError(), eZImageType::classAltTextRequired()).
- Updated: ezjscore/run reads the policy omit list through expPolicyOmitList when the kernel has
  it (idea from LoveStack commit 98854ab935).
- Updated: ezjscore/call answers a PHP Error in a server function with a generic error text and
  logs the details, instead of breaking the JSON response.
- Updated: the module definition reads its function list without ezjscore.ini (an inactive
  extension, a test), and htmlspecialchars() is called with explicit flags, which gives the same
  output on PHP 8.0 as on 8.1 and later.
- Added: settings/rad.ini.append.php declares the server function registry for the extension
  point survey of Exponential.
- Updated: Version 1.6.0 in ezinfo.php and extension.xml.


# 1.5.0
- Removed YUI: the YUI 2 and YUI 3 libraries (design/standard/lib/yui), the packer keys
  ezjsc::yui2, ezjsc::yui3, ezjsc::yui3io and their config functions (yui2conf, yui3conf),
  the [YUI3] settings and the yui entries of ExternalScripts, LocalScripts and
  LocalScriptBasePath. PreferredLibrary is jquery. Code that still requires ezjsc::yui*
  must move to jQuery (ezjsc::jquery, ezjsc::jqueryio) or Exponential UI (extension expui).


